    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "Two factors of $403$, namely $13$ and $31$, can each be written by reversing the digits of the other. Find three other numbers with this property.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Sample answers: $574=14\\times41$, $1300=25\\times52$, $1729=19\\times91$.",
      "worked": "Choose three pairs of two-digit numbers whose digits are reversals of each other, then multiply each pair.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}14\\times41&=14\\times40+14\\\\14\\times41&=574\\\\25\\times52&=25\\times50+25\\times2\\\\25\\times52&=1300\\\\19\\times91&=19\\times90+19\\\\19\\times91&=1729\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $574$, $1300$ and $1729$ each have two factors whose digits are reversals of each other.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
